  "discussion": "No big updates are expected this morning. A small, north-northwest swell peaking this morning will provide a small bump to north and west-facing shores that will fade through the day. Tiny surf is anticipated on Friday. Another small north- northwest swell is forecast to arrive and build on Saturday, peaking Saturday night into Sunday, with a larger (advisory level) and longer lived northwest swell expected next Tuesday. An even larger northwest swell is possible later in the week. Rough surf along east-facing shores will hold near seasonal averages today, then increase slightly for Friday and Saturday as trade winds strengthen. Mainly small background level surf is expected for south- facing shores during the next several days. A small, long-period swell looks to bring a bump to south shore surf on Friday.",
